.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Digest::BMW \- Perl interface to the Blue Midnight Wish digest algorithm
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 2
\&    # Functional interface
\&    use Digest::BMW qw(bmw_256 bmw_256_hex bmw_256_base64);
\&
\&    $digest = bmw_256($data);
\&    $digest = bmw_256_hex($data);
\&    $digest = bmw_256_base64($data);
\&
\&    # Object\-oriented interface
\&    use Digest::BMW;
\&
\&    $ctx = Digest::BMW\->new(256);
\&
\&    $ctx\->add($data);
\&    $ctx\->addfile(*FILE);
\&
\&    $digest = $ctx\->digest;
\&    $digest = $ctx\->hexdigest;
\&    $digest = $ctx\->b64digest;
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
The \f(CW\*(C`Digest::BMW\*(C'\fR module provides an interface to the Blue Midnight Wish
message digest algorithm. Blue Midgnight Wish is a candidate in the NIST
SHA\-3 competition.
.PP
This interface follows the conventions set forth by the \f(CW\*(C`Digest\*(C'\fR module.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.IX Header "FUNCTIONS"
The following functions are provided by the \f(CW\*(C`Digest::BMW\*(C'\fR module. None of
these functions are exported by default.
.SS "bmw_224($data, ...)"
.IX Subsection "bmw_224($data, ...)"
.SS "bmw_256($data, ...)"
.IX Subsection "bmw_256($data, ...)"
.SS "bmw_384($data, ...)"
.IX Subsection "bmw_384($data, ...)"
.SS "bmw_512($data, ...)"
.IX Subsection "bmw_512($data, ...)"
Logically joins the arguments into a single string, and returns its BMW
digest encoded as a binary string.
.SS "bmw_224_hex($data, ...)"
.IX Subsection "bmw_224_hex($data, ...)"
.SS "bmw_256_hex($data, ...)"
.IX Subsection "bmw_256_hex($data, ...)"
.SS "bmw_384_hex($data, ...)"
.IX Subsection "bmw_384_hex($data, ...)"
.SS "bmw_512_hex($data, ...)"
.IX Subsection "bmw_512_hex($data, ...)"
Logically joins the arguments into a single string, and returns its BMW
digest encoded as a hexadecimal string.
.SS "bmw_224_base64($data, ...)"
.IX Subsection "bmw_224_base64($data, ...)"
.SS "bmw_256_base64($data, ...)"
.IX Subsection "bmw_256_base64($data, ...)"
.SS "bmw_384_base64($data, ...)"
.IX Subsection "bmw_384_base64($data, ...)"
.SS "bmw_512_base64($data, ...)"
.IX Subsection "bmw_512_base64($data, ...)"
Logically joins the arguments into a single string, and returns its BMW
digest encoded as a Base64 string, without any trailing padding.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
The object-oriented interface to \f(CW\*(C`Digest::BMW\*(C'\fR is identical to that
described by \f(CW\*(C`Digest\*(C'\fR, except for the following:
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 1
\&    $bmw = Digest::BMW\->new(256)
.Ve
.PP
The constructor requires the algorithm to be specified. It must be one of:
224, 256, 384, 512.
.SS algorithm
.IX Subsection "algorithm"
.SS hashsize
.IX Subsection "hashsize"
Returns the algorithm used by the object.
